    "physical_description": "Man's sarong of checkered silk in orange, green, black and white. ",
    "summary": "Men in Laos wore a plaid silk sarong to attend their Buddhist ordinations or weddings. The checked pattern is an indicator of manhood. Tai weavers cleverly used two-coloured twisted yarns (here, red-yellow, green-yellow) as weft threads to create a shimmering effect, adding interests to the simple plain weave.",
